        "winnerId": "dragonfly",
        "headline": "Dragonfly 1.41M ops/s at the lowest p99 (0.45 ms); KiviDB 1.46M (0.46 ms), the most ops/s on every pass; Redis 182K (2.03 ms); Valkey 180K (2.04 ms)",
        "summary": "SET/GET mix (1:10) at pipeline depth 1 with 100-byte values, 200 connections. The section ranks on p99, and Dragonfly's median was 16 µs lower than KiviDB's, inside both engines' range across passes (0.407 to 0.511 ms and 0.423 to 0.535 ms). KiviDB's throughput lead is outside its range: its slowest pass, 1.44M ops/s, beat Dragonfly's fastest, 1.41M. Redis and Valkey were within 1% of each other at about an eighth of that throughput, and client CPU stayed under 40% on every pass."
      },
