        "headline": "Dragonfly 398K ops/s at the lowest p99 (0.91 ms); KiviDB 398K (0.95 ms), both at the network ceiling; Valkey 108K (3.49 ms); Redis 107K (3.52 ms)",
        "summary": "SET/GET mix (1:10) at pipeline depth 1 with 10 KB values, 200 connections. Dragonfly and KiviDB delivered 397,525 and 397,526 ops/s, 29.6 Gbit/s of values into the client against the instances' 30 Gbit/s rating, so this section can't separate them. Their p99s swung by more than half the median between passes (0.799 to 1.335 ms and 0.775 to 1.279 ms), and the 40 µs between the medians is well inside that. Both ran 3.7 times the throughput of Redis and Valkey at about a quarter of their p99, and Redis and Valkey were within 1% of each other."
